Summary: Per-program extra command-line arguments from the registry (CommandLineAppend)
Category: system
Kind: feature
Origin: reconstructed
  Version: Sikarugir 10.0_8
  Binary: Sikarugir WS12WineSikarugir10.0_8 kernelbase.dll (x86_64)
  Functions: sikarugir_append_command_line, inlined into
    CreateProcessInternalW (x86_64 0x174015cc8-0x174015ed6)
  Note: no published source; behaviour read from the compiled binary
  Changes: the lookup runs after the CEF flags
    (kernelbase-cef-append-flags), so a user's switches come last and win
    (10.0_8 runs it before them); still before the launcher replacement,
    so the key is looked up by the name before any replacement, as in
    10.0_8. REG_EXPAND_SZ values are expanded (10.0_8 ignores them)
Upstream: no
Why: Lets a user or a host add a program's options without editing its
 shortcut. Set the value CommandLineAppend (REG_SZ, or REG_EXPAND_SZ to
 expand environment variables) under
 HKCU\Software\Wine\AppDefaults\<exe file name> (e.g. eldenring.exe); when
 a Windows process creates a process from that exe, the value is appended
 to its command line after a space, and a FIXME is logged. It comes after
 the flags kernelbase-cef-append-flags adds, so for a switch both set,
 Chromium takes the user's. It doesn't apply to the process `wine <exe>`
 starts directly: start it with `wine start` instead. For a launcher that
 kernelbase-replace-launchers swaps for the game, set it for the
 launcher's name.
Programs: none known
Enable: reg HKCU\Software\Wine\AppDefaults\<exe file name>\CommandLineAppend = <arguments> (REG_SZ or REG_EXPAND_SZ) (per program; processes started by CreateProcess, not the one `wine <exe>` starts)
Messages: "Sikarugir: appended %s to the command line of %s" (FIXME, channel
 process; WINEDEBUG=-all or fixme-all hides it)
Risk: adds the value's text to the program's command line; any program in
 the prefix can set it for another exe (same user and prefix, so no
 boundary is crossed)
Uncertain: limits copied from 10.0_8: exe names of 260+ characters are
 skipped and values over 2048 bytes (1023 characters), or over 1023
 characters once expanded, are ignored.
Expects before it: kernelbase-replace-launchers (context),
 kernelbase-cef-append-flags (context)
Related: ntdll-cef-command-line-args; Epic Games Launcher's and Ubisoft
 Connect's CEF take switches from the command line only with it
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-26: runs after the CEF flags (review decision
 15); accepts REG_EXPAND_SZ
 10.0: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T013940 and T024442 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed

